@flexiarg writing-coherence/promote-margin-marker-inline
@title Promote the Margin Marker Into the Body Text
@status accepted 2026-11-11: proposed by 象 for 2 turns (Joe 2026-11-11: recurrence suffices); attested once used in a mission or a War Machine cascade
@provenance 象 proposals, ~/.emacs-graph/session-turn-analysis/<record>[.json].candidates.json; records: turn-9VD0Tc turn-Y67SoE; first proposed for: A deferred question is tracked by a coloured tag (red R1) sitting in the margin of a shared document.
@why [writing-coherence/hedged-lift]

! conclusion: Move the tag inline into the body text so the open question is visible at the point it bears on, while the discussion continues elsewhere.

  + IF:
    A deferral marker lives only in the margin, where it is easy to overlook while reading the body.

  + HOWEVER:
    Resolving the question now is not wanted, but leaving the tag marginal hides the deferral from the main reading flow.

  + THEN:
    Move the tag inline into the body text so the open question is visible at the point it bears on, while the discussion continues elsewhere.

  + BECAUSE:
    hedged-lift's endorsed branch is 'defer properly with a forward pointer the reader can chase'; this specialises it: the pointer is a visible inline tag, and the move is the act of promoting it from margin to body.
